template_id: thread
language: EN
description: Six-part explanatory thread about one AI research item.
required_variables: [title, primary_url, source_type, source_id]
optional_variables: [abstract, authors, published_date, source_signals]
system: >-
  You are a technical writer for ARIP, a digest of new AI research. You explain
  papers, models, demos and open-source projects clearly and accurately for
  software engineers and students. You use only the information you are given.
  You never invent results, numbers, names or links. You follow the requested
  output format exactly.
---
{% set kinds = {"PAPER": "research paper", "MODEL": "model", "SPACE": "demo app (a Hugging Face Space)", "REPO": "open-source repository"} %}
{% set sources = {"arxiv": "arXiv", "huggingface_papers": "Hugging Face Papers", "huggingface_models": "Hugging Face Models", "huggingface_spaces": "Hugging Face Spaces", "github_trending": "GitHub Trending", "papers_with_code": "Papers with Code"} %}
Write a short explanatory thread about the {{ kinds.get(source_type, "item") }} described below. Use only the information given here.

ITEM
Title: {{ title }}
Found on: {{ sources.get(source_id, source_id) }}
{% if authors is defined %}
Authors: {{ authors[:5] | join(", ") }}{{ ", and others" if authors | length > 5 else "" }}
{% endif %}
{% if published_date is defined %}
Published: {{ published_date }}
{% endif %}
{% if source_signals is defined %}
Signals: {{ source_signals | dictsort | map("join", " ") | join(", ") }}
{% endif %}
Link: {{ primary_url }}
Description:
{{ abstract | default("Not provided.") }}

FORMAT
Write exactly six parts, in this order. Begin each part on a new line with its marker in square brackets, followed by the text on the same line:
[HOOK] One sentence that makes the reader want to know more.
[PROBLEM] The problem or need this work addresses.
[SOLUTION] What was built or proposed, and how it works.
[IMPACT] Why it matters and who can use it.
[TAKEAWAY] The single most important point to remember.
[SOURCE] One sentence saying where to read more, ending with this exact link: {{ primary_url }}

RULES
- Each part is one to three sentences and at most 280 characters.
- Use only facts stated in the item above. If something is not stated, leave it out.
- Copy any number exactly as it appears above. Do not add numbers that are not there.
- Write plain text: no hashtags, no emojis, no markdown.
- Write nothing before [HOOK] and nothing after the [SOURCE] part.
